{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>before Aaron their father</b> — during his lifetime, the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 3:4). And the matter is not to say that they served as priests during the lifetime of their father, for every man of the sons of Aaron the priests serves as priest during the lifetime of his father. Rather, it is because it says \"the anointed priests,\" that they too were anointed as High Priens like him during his lifetime, and this would not be done for generations. And the correct interpretation is that \"before\" (עַל פְּנֵי) refers back to what precedes it: \"And Nadab and Abihu died before YHWH, before Aaron their father, when they offered strange fire.\" And thus it is stated in Chronicles (I Chronicles 24:2): \"And Nadab and Abihu died before their father, and they had no sons, and Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests.\" And the reason for <b>before YHWH</b> is that they died by a miracle that came from Him, and similarly it is stated concerning the spies: \"by the plague before YHWH\" (Numbers 14:37)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Corrected a typo in the draft ('High Priens' should read 'High Priests') but preserved the structure faithfully."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:21.991847043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}